---
import { Callout, Link } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro'

const settingsExample = `{
  "lsp": {
    "dep-beacon": {
      "settings": {
        "checkVulnerabilities": true,
        "includePrerelease": false,
        "registryUrl": "https://registry.npmjs.org"
      }
    }
  }
}`
---

<Docs title="Zed Extension" description="Zed features provided by Dep Beacon through the Language Server Protocol.">
  <h1>Dep Beacon for Zed</h1>
  <p>
    Dep Beacon brings npm dependency intelligence to Zed through the Language Server Protocol. Open `package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or `pnpm-workspace.yml` to see dependency signals in your editor.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the command palette in Zed.</li>
    <li>Run `zed: extensions`.</li>
    <li>Search for `Dep Beacon` and select Install.</li>
    <li>Open a supported manifest.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>CodeLens shows the current dependency status above supported entries.</li>
    <li>Diagnostics identify outdated, invalid, missing, and vulnerable packages.</li>
    <li>Quick fixes apply patch, minor, major, and latest update targets.</li>
    <li>Document links open dependency names on npm.</li>
    <li>Default and named pnpm catalogs resolve before dependency analysis.</li>
    <li>Optional OSV.dev checks add vulnerability severity to dependency diagnostics.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Settings</h2>
  <p>
    Configure the language server under `lsp.dep-beacon.settings` in your Zed settings file.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{settingsExample}</code></pre>
  <ul>
    <li>`checkVulnerabilities` defaults to `true`.</li>
    <li>`includePrerelease` defaults to `false`.</li>
    <li>`registryUrl` defaults to the public npm registry.</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout class="docs-callout">
    <strong>Editor differences:</strong>
    <span>Zed does not currently expose APIs equivalent to VS Code inline decorations or install-on-save, so those features remain VS Code-only.</span>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <p>
    The Zed adapter and language server are available in the <Link href="https://github.com/santi020k/dep-beacon/tree/main/packages/zed-dep-beacon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dep Beacon repository</Link>.
  </p>
</Docs>
